# The Fitting subgroup is the join of the `p`-cores

This file proves that the Fitting subgroup of a finite group is the join of its `p`-cores
`O_p(G) = pCore p G` (`fitting_eq_iSup_pCore`), and deduces that the Fitting subgroup is
nilpotent (`fitting_nilpotent`), the Fitting subgroup being *defined* as the supremum of all
normal nilpotent subgroups.

## Main results

* `le_iSup_pCore_of_isNilpotent_normal` : a nilpotent normal subgroup `X` of `G` is contained in
  the join of the `O_p(G)` for `p ∣ |X|`;
* `fitting_eq_iSup_pCore` : `F(G) = ⨆_{p ∣ |G|} O_p(G)`;
* `fitting_nilpotent` : `F(G)` is nilpotent (i.e. `F(G)` is the *largest* nilpotent normal
  subgroup).

The nilpotency of the join of normal subgroups of pairwise coprime order is
`Work.Fitting.isNilpotent_iSup_of_normal_pgroups`
(`Submission/Work/Fitting/isNilpotent_iSup_of_normal_pgroups.lean`), and the fact that a finite
nilpotent group is generated by its Sylow subgroups is `Work.Fitting.iSup_sylow_eq_top`
(`Submission/Work/Fitting/iSup_sylow_eq_top.lean`).
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.Fitting.Basic
import Submission.Work.Fitting.PCore
import Submission.Work.Fitting.iSup_sylow_eq_top
import Submission.Work.Fitting.isNilpotent_iSup_of_normal_pgroups
